From: Alexbob0 <190955252+Alexbob0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:44:00 +0100
Subject: The Runs API reports each model call's usage as it ends (model.usage)

Each model call's provider usage goes to agent.call_usage_callback once the session counters hold it; a run of
POST /v1/runs turns it into a model.usage event (the call, then the run's totals so far). On v0.22.5 both run
paths emit it: the direct one (the run's own agent) and the session authority's (wire_api_observers, totals counted
from the turn's start since that agent is the session's cached one). The authority's run.completed usage keeps the
turn's cache_read_tokens / cache_write_tokens beside input and output.

BipAgents patch, documented in hermes/patches/README.md of the BipAgents repository.

Bip-Patch: 0020-runs-model-usage-per-call
